        {
          "type": "notebook_cells",
          "attributes": {
            "definition": {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "## 2. Timeline\n\nUse UTC and be specific to the minute. Include the moment the first signal existed, not just the moment a human saw it — the gap between those two is usually the most actionable finding in the whole document.\n\n| Time (UTC) | Event | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| | First measurable deviation | Monitor / graph |\n| | First alert fired | Monitor name |\n| | First human acknowledged | |\n| | Incident declared | |\n| | Root cause identified | |\n| | Mitigation applied | |\n| | Customer impact ended | |\n| | Incident resolved | |\n\n**Detection gap:** _first deviation → first alert_\n\n**Response gap:** _first alert → human acknowledged_\n\nIf the detection gap is large, the finding is about monitoring coverage. If the response gap is large, the finding is about routing and priority. These are different problems with different fixes, and conflating them produces action items that help with neither."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "notebook_cells",
          "attributes": {
            "definition": {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "## 3. Which services were involved\n\nAdjust the service filters below to the services in question. Latency and error rate together are usually enough to establish the direction of causation: the service that degraded *first* is rarely the one people noticed first.\n\nRemember that trace metrics are namespaced by entry-span name, so the query depends on the runtime — `trace.fastify.request` for the Node services, `trace.fastapi.request` for the Python services, `trace.http.request` for the Go services. See 02-TECH-STACK.md § 5.2."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "notebook_cells",
          "attributes": {
            "graph_size": "l",
            "split_by": { "keys": [], "tags": [] },
            "definition": {
              "type": "timeseries",
              "title": "p95 latency by service — all three runtimes",
              "show_legend": true,
              "legend_layout": "auto",
              "legend_columns": ["avg", "max", "value"],
              "yaxis": { "include_zero": false },
              "requests": [
                {
                  "display_type": "line",
                  "response_format": "timeseries",
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "node",
                      "query": "p95:trace.fastify.request{env:demo} by {service}"
                    },
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "python",
                      "query": "p95:trace.fastapi.request{env:demo} by {service}"
                    },
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "go",
                      "query": "p95:trace.http.request{env:demo} by {service}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "formulas": [
